QWEN35_USER = "[FORMAT:TSV] Transcris chaque ligne de texte visible dans cette image avec sa localisation.\n\nOutput a ```tsv code block. For EACH physical line of text, write ONE row:\n  <transcription><TAB><xmin><TAB><ymin><TAB><xmax><TAB><ymax><TAB><angle>\n\nCoordinates are integers in [0, 1000] (0 = top/left edge, 1000 = bottom/right edge). Angle is an integer in degrees. No header row.\n\nExample:\n```tsv\nLe sieur Dupont vous écrit\t52\t38\t680\t61\t0\nau sujet de la requête\t52\t68\t590\t91\t-1\ndu 14 janvier 1743.\t52\t98\t430\t121\t0\n```\n\nRules:\n1. One physical line of text → exactly one row. Never merge two lines into one row.\n2. A tab separates the 6 fields. A tab must NEVER appear inside the transcription.\n   Wrong: Dupont\tDurand\t...  →  Right: Dupont Durand\t52\t38\t680\t61\t0\n3. Use only the straight apostrophe character ' in transcriptions; never use ’, ʼ, `, or other apostrophe variants.\n4. Table cells: each cell is its own row with its own bounding box.\n5. Never output the same physical line twice."